# GameTimer phone API (Phase 1). Works with the VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client .http format.
# 1. Settings tab: turn on "Phone control", click "Connect phone", copy the code from the URL.
# 2. Run the pairing request below, then paste the returned token into @token.
# Errors: { "error": "<code>" } with 400 (bad input) or 409 (wrong timer state); 401 without a valid token.

@host = http://localhost:5123
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Pair (one-time code from the QR link, valid 2 minutes)
POST {{host}}/pair
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "ABCD2345", "name": "PowerShell" }

### Status: state (notStarted|running|stopped|expired), mode, remainingSeconds, targetTime, action, zone,
### scheduleStatus (off|allowed|outsideWindow|dayDisabled|limitReached), scheduleAvailableSeconds, usedSecondsToday
GET {{host}}/api/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Start: mode "interval" (hours 0-23, minutes 0-59) or "absolute" (time of day)
POST {{host}}/api/timer/start
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "interval", "hours": 0, "minutes": 30 }

### Extend: positive adds, negative removes; never below zero (zero expires the timer)
POST {{host}}/api/timer/extend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "minutes": 15 }

### Stop (also cancels a pending shutdown)
POST {{host}}/api/timer/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Settings
GET {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update settings: every field optional; action shutdown|lock|logoff, thresholds 1-1440 min,
### colors #RRGGBB, language en|ru, alertPoints replaces the whole list
PUT {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "lock", "redThreshold": 5, "alertPoints": [ { "minutes": 5, "enabled": true }, { "minutes": 1, "enabled": true } ] }

### Schedule: { enabled, week[7] }. week is indexed by weekday 0=Sunday..6=Saturday.
### Each day: allowed, limitMinutes (0=no budget), windowStartMinutes, windowEndMinutes (0..1440; 0 & 1440 = all day).
GET {{host}}/api/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update schedule: all 7 days required; minute fields 0..1440. Takes effect immediately (may lock the PC).
PUT {{host}}/api/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": true, "week": [
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 120, "windowStartMinutes": 540, "windowEndMinutes": 1260 },
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 60,  "windowStartMinutes": 900, "windowEndMinutes": 1200 },
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 60,  "windowStartMinutes": 900, "windowEndMinutes": 1200 },
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 60,  "windowStartMinutes": 900, "windowEndMinutes": 1200 },
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 60,  "windowStartMinutes": 900, "windowEndMinutes": 1200 },
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 60,  "windowStartMinutes": 900, "windowEndMinutes": 1200 },
  { "allowed": true, "limitMinutes": 120, "windowStartMinutes": 540, "windowEndMinutes": 1260 }
] }

### WebSocket push events: ws://localhost:5123/ws  (watch them with docs/ws-watch.ps1)
# Auth: "Authorization: Bearer <token>" on the upgrade request, or (browsers) a first message
#   { "type": "auth", "token": "<token>" } within 5 s. Failure: close 1008 "unauthorized" / "auth_timeout".
# Server messages (JSON, field "type"):
#   hello {status, settings}                once, right after auth
#   started | stopped | expired {status}     timer state changes (stopped also covers reset)
#   tick {status}                           every 5 s while running
#   alert {minutes, status}                 an alert point was reached
#   extended {minutes, status}              time added / removed
#   settingsChanged {settings}              only when the API-visible settings changed
#   schedule {status}                       the schedule allowed/blocked state or the day's allowance changed
# Server closes: 1008 "revoked" (device removed), 1001 "server_stopping". Max 10 connections (503).

### Paired devices
GET {{host}}/api/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoke a device
DELETE {{host}}/api/devices/DEVICE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
